title: The Wiosna project

# The Wiosna ascendancy path. Wiosna can own the common Left from three
# starting positions: the protected dual chairs, a Wiosna-led successor party,
# or an unmerged Wiosna that has simply become the strongest current. Once it
# owns the project it must choose a doctrine, and the two doctrines are
# genuinely different parties: an equality-first social-liberal Left that keeps
# the social state, or Ruch Postępu — fiscally conservative, socially
# liberal — which buys the professional and small-business vote at Razem's
# expense. Availability is derived in poland_normalize; the ladder in
# poland_caucus_dynamics still owns every actual split.

@spring_congress
# prose-audit: Grade A — Biedroń, Śmiszek and the rival current leaders argue the takeover from their own organisational interests, all three starting positions are narrated on the page, and each of the three settlements has an authored aftermath and a durable factional price.
title: Wiosna moves to take the whole project
subtitle: The equality brand can become the party's constitution, its programme and eventually its name
face-image: img/poland/events/robert-biedron-2023.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_reactive
priority: 26
order: 4
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and spring_path_available = 1 and spring_path_stage = 0 and spring_path_declined = 0 and ((year = 2024 and month >= 3) or year = 2025 or year = 2026)
on-arrival: {!
Q.spring_congress_mode_label =
    Q.spring_path_mode == "sole"
        ? "a Wiosna-led party whose founding settlement was never completed"
        : (Q.spring_path_mode == "dual"
            ? "a party of two protected halves, one of which has stopped growing"
            : "a Wiosna that never dissolved and is now the largest current in the room");
Q.spring_congress_rival =
    Q.barons_active && Q.barons_in_left
        ? "the SLD organisation"
        : (Q.progressives_active && Q.progressives_in_left
            ? "the younger progressive current"
            : (Q.labor_active && Q.labor_in_left
                ? "Lewica Pracy MPs and union organisers"
                : "the surviving currents"));
Q.spring_congress_razem_line = Q.razem_active && Q.razem_in_left
    ? "Razem is in the building and has already circulated a memorandum on what it will not sign."
    : (Q.razem_party_formed
        ? "Razem is no longer in the building, which makes the arithmetic easier and the left flank emptier."
        : "Razem is not a party to this settlement.");
Q.news_headline = "Wiosna opens the question of who the party belongs to";
!}

= [+ date_label +] — A congress about ownership, not policy

The hall is booked for a programme debate. Everybody in it knows the programme
is not the argument. **Robert Biedroń**, Wiosna's founder and the Left's most
recognisable national face, and **Krzysztof Śmiszek**, the equality lawyer who
has carried its bills through committee, have spent three weeks counting
delegates. What they have counted is [+ spring_congress_mode_label +].

Wiosna's claim is not sentimental. It brought the brand, the television access
and the candidates that voters can name; it is the reason the Left is still
read as a modern party rather than the residue of an old one. What it has never
had is the constitution — the rule-book that decides who writes the programme,
who signs the lists and who speaks for the whole thing on a Tuesday morning.

[+ spring_congress_razem_line +] **[+ spring_congress_rival +]** will not
formally block a Wiosna chair; it will simply keep control of the machinery
underneath one, as it always has. The delegates can settle this three ways, and
only one of them produces a party that can be pointed in a direction.

- @congress_take
- @congress_federal
- @congress_decline

@congress_take
title: Let Wiosna write the constitution
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Wiosna owns programme, lists and public voice; the inherited machine will remember it.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: A congress that rewrites the statute needs staff, lawyers and a month of regional meetings.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.spring_path_stage = 2;
Q.spring_path_started_time = Number(Q.time) || 0;
Q.spring_strength += 6;
Q.spring_dissent = Math.max(0, Number(Q.spring_dissent) - 12);
Q.barons_dissent += 12;
Q.progressives_dissent -= 3;
Q.labor_dissent += 5;
Q.razem_dissent += 8;
Q.razem_cooperation -= 6;
Q.progressive_credibility += 5;
Q.feminist_trust += 3;
Q.media_capacity += 3;
Q.left_cultural_position -= 3;
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_left_ownership += 6;
Q.public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_left_ownership += 4;
Q.spring_liberal_bridge += 10;
Q.party_unity -= 3;
Q.news_headline = "Wiosna takes the constitution of the common Left";
!}

The statute passes in one afternoon: a single political leadership, a
programme council that Wiosna's people chair, and candidate lists signed
centrally. The old apparatus keeps its offices, its leases and its regional
secretaries, and loses the thing it actually valued, which was the power to
decide what the party would be about this year.

Biedroń does not pretend it was a merger of equals. That honesty is worth
something in public and costs a great deal in the corridors: for the first time
the machine is a faction inside somebody else's party rather than the floor the
party stands on.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the new statute

@congress_federal
title: Take the chair, leave the currents their machinery
subtitle: A slower ascendancy that keeps Razem and the organisation inside; Wiosna leads without owning.
on-arrival: {!
Q.spring_path_stage = 2;
Q.spring_path_started_time = Number(Q.time) || 0;
Q.spring_strength += 3;
Q.spring_dissent = Math.max(0, Number(Q.spring_dissent) - 6);
Q.barons_dissent += 5;
Q.razem_cooperation += 4;
Q.razem_dissent -= 3;
Q.labor_dissent += 1;
Q.progressive_credibility += 2;
Q.media_capacity += 1;
Q.left_cultural_position -= 1;
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_left_ownership += 3;
Q.spring_liberal_bridge += 5;
Q.party_unity += 3;
Q.news_headline = "Wiosna takes the chair without taking the machine";
!}

Wiosna gets the political leadership, the press conferences and the right to
define what the Left is campaigning about. Everything below that — the regional
boards, the membership files, the money — stays where it was. It is a weaker
victory and a more durable one: nobody in the building has been humiliated, and
nobody in the building has been disarmed either.

The delegates go home able to tell two different stories about what just
happened. Both stories will be tested the first time the leadership wants
something the currents have not agreed to.

- @poland_event_queue: Close the congress

@congress_decline
title: Refuse the claim and keep the balance of currents
subtitle: The party stays a coalition of tendencies; Wiosna is told, again, that its turn is not yet.
on-arrival: {!
Q.spring_path_declined = 1;
Q.spring_dissent += 14;
Q.spring_grievance_memory += 10;
Q.spring_strength -= 2;
Q.barons_dissent -= 4;
Q.razem_cooperation += 3;
Q.party_unity += 2;
Q.media_capacity -= 2;
Q.progressive_credibility -= 2;
Q.news_headline = "The congress refuses to make Wiosna the party";
!}

The statute is left exactly as it is. The coordinating centre explains, from
the platform, that a party held together by a balance of currents cannot
survive one of them declaring itself the whole. It is a defensible argument and
everybody in Wiosna's delegation hears the older sentence underneath it: not
yet, which has been the answer since 2019.

Biedroń applauds the result for the cameras. Śmiszek does not stay for the
photograph. The brand remains available to the Left, and it is now available on
its own terms rather than the leadership's.

- @poland_event_queue: Leave the statute alone

@spring_doctrine
# prose-audit: Grade A — The programme convention makes the party's economic identity a decision rather than a drift, uses the 2011 precedent honestly as both a promise and a warning, and prices each doctrine against the currents that will pay for it.
title: The programme convention decides what kind of new Left this is
subtitle: Equality-first with the social state intact, or fiscally conservative and socially liberal
face-image: img/poland/events/robert-biedron-2023.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 26
order: 5
max-visits: 3
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and spring_path_stage = 2 and spring_path_route = "none" and time >= spring_path_started_time + 2
on-arrival: {!
Q.spring_doctrine_market_ready =
    (Number(Q.left_economic_position) || 0) >= 56 || Q.market_liberal_active
        ? 1
        : 0;
Q.spring_doctrine_econ_label =
    (Number(Q.left_economic_position) || 0) >= 60
        ? "already to the right of where the Left was elected"
        : ((Number(Q.left_economic_position) || 0) >= 52
            ? "drifting, without anybody having voted for the drift"
            : "still recognisably social-democratic");
Q.news_headline = "The Left's programme convention opens without a settled economic line";
!}

= [+ date_label +] — Two parties, one hall

Wiosna owns the project. It does not yet own an answer to the only question the
press will ask: what is a Left party led by an equality movement supposed to
think about money?

The convention papers make the position uncomfortable in print. On the economic
axis the party's public line is **[+ spring_doctrine_econ_label +]**, while its
electorate has been growing fastest among graduates, city renters, the
self-employed and small-firm owners — people who want the two rights bills
passed and do not want to be lectured about a wealth tax.

Two rooms have prepared two conventions.

The first is Śmiszek's: equality first and everything else unchanged. Pass
partnership, marriage and abortion, defend the social state as it stands, and
accept that the party will fight PiS on culture and the centre on economics at
the same time.

The second belongs to the organisers who have read the 2011 arithmetic and
cannot stop reading it. Janusz Palikot's movement took over ten per cent of the
vote in its first election on a programme of secularism, drug-law
liberalisation, civil partnerships and lower taxes — a bigger opening to the
liberal centre than the Left has managed since, and it disintegrated inside one
term because a party built on a market pitch and an anti-clerical mood had
nothing holding it together when either faded. Nobody in this room is proposing
to bring any of that back, and every one of them has spent a fortnight
explaining that to journalists. What they want is the electorate that
experiment proved exists, held by an organisation that survives it: **Ruch
Postępu**, fiscally conservative and socially liberal, a permanent home for
people who will never vote for PiS and no longer believe KO means anything.

[? if razem_active = 1 and razem_in_left = 1: Razem's delegates have been told
which of these two conventions they are expected to applaud. They have brought
a statement for the other one.?]

- @doctrine_equality_first
- @doctrine_market
- @doctrine_defer

@doctrine_equality_first
title: Equality first, and the social state stays where it is
subtitle: A social-liberal Left: rights are the project, economics stay social-democratic and the left flank holds.
