The convention adopts the shortest programme the party has published in twenty
years. Two bills are named with dates. Nothing in the welfare architecture is
opened, repriced or apologised for, which costs the leadership its chance to
be praised as serious by the business press and buys it a left flank that will
not walk out in the middle of a rights campaign.

[? if razem_active = 1 and razem_in_left = 1: Razem's delegates vote for it
without enthusiasm and say so from the floor: an equality party that does not
touch their economics is one they can share a list with, and one they will not
defend for free.?] The party is now, on paper and in public, a movement for two
laws — which means it will be judged on whether it gets them.

- @poland_event_queue: Adopt the equality programme

