Q.news_headline = "The Left relaunches as a fiscally conservative, socially liberal party";
!}

The convention votes for the sentence the leadership has been testing in
private for a year, and once it is voted it belongs to the party for good:
fiscally conservative, socially liberal. **Ruch Postępu** — simpler taxes, a
smaller state, no lectures about how anyone earns their money, and an
absolutely uncompromising line on marriage, abortion, the Church and the police.

It works immediately in exactly the places the polling said it would. Graduate
professionals who have voted KO out of habit, self-employed builders and
designers who resent every form they file, city renters under thirty-five who
find Konfederacja's freedom talk attractive until it reaches women and gay
people — all of them hear a party that is finally speaking to them without
apologising.

[? if razem_active = 1 and razem_in_left = 1: Razem's delegation leaves before
the vote is announced. Zandberg's statement is one paragraph and contains the
word "liquidation".?][? if labor_active = 1 and labor_in_left = 1: The labour
current stays in the hall, physically, and stops speaking to the press on the
leadership's behalf that evening.?] Somebody has tried a version of this pitch
in Polish politics before, and everyone in the room knows how long it lasted.

- @poland_event_queue: Take the new line to the country

@doctrine_defer
title: Refuse to choose and run on both halves
subtitle: Keeps the party together for now at the cost of a line nobody can repeat back to you.
on-arrival: {!
