Q.public_trust -= 2;
Q.news_headline = "The programme convention closes without an economic line";
!}

The final text keeps both conventions inside one document: the rights bills
with dates, the social state defended in principle, the tax system described as
needing "simplification" in a sentence that survived four drafts precisely
because it commits to nothing.

Nobody walks out. The problem arrives later and quietly, when journalists,
donors and the party's own candidates each decide for themselves which half was
the real one, and start saying so on television.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the compromise text

@spring_two_bills
