= [+ date_label +] — The arithmetic of two laws

The party owns the issue. Śmiszek's committee has the drafts, the movement has
the mobilisation, and the polling shows the Left credited with the argument
whether or not it ever wins it. What it does not have is two hundred and
thirty-one votes, and it faces **[+ spring_bills_palace +]**.

The available majorities are not the same majority. Civil partnership can pass
with conservative abstentions; marriage and adoption need the liberal centre to
vote for something it has spent fifteen years promising and deferring. Abortion
splits the centre differently again, and every day the two questions are debated
together is a day the opposition gets to talk about children.

Three ways to spend the next parliamentary year.

- @bills_liberal_bloc
- @bills_sequence
- @bills_country

