Signature stalls outside every voivodeship office, a bus, and two months of
being the only party willing to hold the argument in towns where holding it is
unpleasant. Support moves — slowly, and further than the parliamentary
arithmetic did.

So does the opposition. The bishops' conference issues a letter, the public
broadcaster finds three families a week to interview, and the backlash number
in the party's own polling climbs alongside the support number. The bills are
now unavoidable rather than agreed.

- @poland_event_queue: Send the campaign out

@spring_concordat
