= [+ date_label +] — What the state pays for

The question arrives, as it always does, through money rather than theology.
The Church Fund, catechism hours inside the school timetable and their teachers'
salaries, chaplaincies in hospitals and barracks: none of it requires a
doctrinal argument, all of it appears in a budget line, and the 1993 Concordat
sits underneath the parts that a ministry cannot simply cancel.

[+ spring_concordat_ministry +]. A party that has made secularism part of its
public identity cannot keep answering this with a shrug, and cannot pretend
that the most satisfying answer is the most achievable one.

- @concordat_treaty
- @concordat_timetable
- @concordat_hold

@concordat_treaty
title: Open the Concordat for renegotiation
subtitle: The maximal position. It will not conclude this term and it will define the next campaign.
on-arrival: {!
