Q.last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary and diplomatic proposal";
Q.last_policy_implementation = 0;
Q.news_headline = "The Left calls for the Concordat to be reopened";
!}

A treaty with the Holy See is renegotiated by a foreign ministry over years, not
by a resolution, and everyone briefing against the idea says so accurately. The
proposal is made anyway, because the point is to establish that the arrangement
is a political choice rather than part of the constitutional furniture.

The Left owns the secular argument completely from this week onward. It also
owns every consequence of it in provincial constituencies where the parish is
still the only institution that has never closed.

- @poland_event_queue: File the resolution

