Q.news_headline = "The Left tables a tax and deregulation package aimed at the self-employed";
!}

One rate band collapsed into another, a contribution ceiling for small business
licences, and a planning regime that stops treating a converted attic as a
national security question. The business press writes about the Left in the
present tense for the first time since the transition. Konfederacja's young
supporters read a party that offers them the same economics without the
homophobia attached.

Inside the building it lands as a declaration of what the party is now for. The
public-sector unions that supplied the Left's canvassers for twenty years are
not persuaded by an argument about invoices, and are not asked to be.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the package

@market_selfemployed
title: Limit it to contribution relief for small business licences
subtitle: The defensible half. It reads as competence rather than conversion, and buys less of everything.
on-arrival: {!
