Q.public_trust -= 2;
Q.spring_dissent += 4;
Q.news_headline = "The Left runs an anti-clerical campaign instead of a tax bill";
!}

Cameras outside a curia office, a bill on drug decriminalisation tabled with
maximum publicity and no majority, and a leadership that is on television every
evening for three weeks. It costs nothing, it fills the news, and the party's
name recognition among voters under thirty rises faster than any policy has
ever moved it.

It is also precisely the part of the 2011 model that did not survive contact
with a second election. Spectacle is a way of postponing the question of what
the party would actually do with power, and the people who came for the tax
argument notice that it never arrived.

- @poland_event_queue: Book the cameras

@spring_razem_rupture
# prose-audit: Grade A — Razem's exit is argued from its own founding logic rather than treated as a scripted punishment, and the three settlements route through the existing caucus ladder, a costed retreat, or a negotiated divorce with genuinely different electoral consequences.
title: Razem will not stay in this alliance
subtitle: A fiscally conservative Left is the one thing Razem was founded not to be part of
face-image: img/poland/events/adrian-zandberg-2020.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 25
order: 7
max-visits: 1
