Q.spring_attack_line = Q.spring_path_route == "market_liberal"
    ? "a party that abandoned workers to chase graduates, run by people who have never worked a shift"
    : "a party that has nothing to say about wages because it only cares about who sleeps with whom";
Q.spring_attack_konf = Q.spring_path_route == "market_liberal"
    ? "Konfederacja's problem is worse: the Left is now openly competing for its young urban voters on tax and the state, without carrying its positions on women and gay people."
    : "Konfederacja is comfortable: it can attack the Left on culture without ever having to discuss its own economics.";
Q.news_headline = "PiS and Konfederacja open a coordinated attack on the Left's new line";
!}

= [+ date_label +] — Being defined by other people

The attack is not improvised. PiS's message discipline has settled on one
sentence repeated by every spokesperson: this is **[+ spring_attack_line +]**.
It is delivered in provincial studios, in parish bulletins and in the
constituencies where the Left's remaining industrial vote lives.

[+ spring_attack_konf +]

The party has three weeks before the framing sets. It can defend the ground it
chose, fight for the ground the radical right thinks it owns, or refuse the
argument and hope the salience falls.

- @counter_rights
- @counter_freedom
- @counter_cool

@counter_rights
title: Defend the chosen ground and escalate on rights
subtitle: Polarise deliberately. The Left's own electorate consolidates; the disputed middle hardens.
on-arrival: {!
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_salience += 7;
Q.public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_salience += 5;
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_backlash += 5;
