Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.psl_relation += 2;
if (Q.left_in_government) Q.government_delivery += 2;
Q.progressives_dissent += 5;
Q.spring_dissent += 4;
Q.feminist_trust -= 3;
Q.progressive_credibility -= 3;
Q.left_poll_momentum -= 0.05;
Q.news_headline = "The Left declines the culture-war framing and talks about delivery";
!}

The leadership decides that answering makes the attack the story, and that a
party with legislation in committee has better uses for a fortnight. Every
interview is turned back to hospitals, contributions and waiting lists.

The temperature falls. So does the party's presence in the argument its own
members care most about, and the currents that have staked everything on the
rights agenda draw the obvious conclusion about what the leadership will defend
when it is expensive.

- @poland_event_queue: Change the subject

@spring_ko_offer
# prose-audit: Grade A — The liberal centre's offer is the real strategic threat to a socially liberal Left, and the three answers separate absorption, a priced alliance and independence with fully authored consequences for the party's seats, brand and reform commitments.
title: The liberal centre makes its offer
subtitle: KO proposes that a party this close to it should stop standing against it
face-image: img/poland/events/donald-tusk-2023.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 25
order: 9
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and spring_path_stage >= 2 and spring_path_route != "none" and spring_liberal_bridge >= 55 and time >= spring_route_time + 6
on-arrival: {!
Q.spring_ko_pitch = Q.spring_path_route == "market_liberal"
    ? "On economics there is now no measurable difference between the two parties, and KO's negotiators say so with the polling attached."
    : "On rights KO's liberal wing already votes with us, and its negotiators would rather own the argument than keep losing seats to the party making it.";
Q.news_headline = "KO opens talks on a common list with the Left";
!}

= [+ date_label +] — The most dangerous conversation

The proposal is put politely and it is not a compliment. **[+ spring_ko_pitch
+]** A common list, protected places for the Left's recognisable names, a
written commitment on the rights bills, and an end to two parties spending the
same money to win the same voters in the same cities.

Every part of it is rational. The trap is also in every part of it: a smaller
partner on a larger party's list stops being a party that voters choose and
becomes a wing that voters tolerate, and the written commitment on the bills is
worth exactly what the larger partner's parliamentary arithmetic makes it worth
after polling day.

- @ko_offer_join
- @ko_offer_price
- @ko_offer_refuse

@ko_offer_join
title: Accept the common list
subtitle: Seats now, independence later. The party becomes a current inside somebody else's project.
on-arrival: {!
Q.ko_relation += 12;
Q.spring_liberal_bridge += 20;
Q.marriage_ko_commitment += 1;
Q.abortion_ko_commitment += 1;
Q.sejm_list_target = "Common list with KO";
Q.sejm_list_has_partners = 1;
Q.sejm_list_negotiation_done = 1;
Q.razem_dissent += 20;
Q.razem_cooperation -= 15;
Q.labor_dissent += 12;
Q.progressives_dissent += 10;
Q.barons_dissent += 14;
Q.spring_dissent += 5;
Q.party_unity -= 8;
Q.left_poll_momentum -= 0.25;
Q.public_trust -= 1;
Q.news_headline = "The Left agrees to stand on a common list with KO";
!}

The agreement is signed with the protected places itemised, which is how
everyone in the room knows what the agreement really is. The Left's leadership
enters the next parliament with a plausible number of deputies and no separate
electoral existence to return to if the arrangement disappoints.

Inside the party the reaction is not ideological, or not only. The regional
organisation understands immediately that a current on somebody else's list
does not need regional organisation, and begins acting accordingly.

- @poland_event_queue: Sign the list agreement

@ko_offer_price
title: Name the price: both bills passed before any list is discussed
subtitle: Cooperation converted into legislation. If they mean it, we get the laws; if not, we get the refusal on record.
on-arrival: {!
Q.marriage_ko_commitment += 2;
Q.abortion_ko_commitment += 1;
Q.ko_accept_rights += 7;
Q.ko_relation += 3;
Q.spring_liberal_bridge += 8;
Q.marriage_reform_progress += 6;
Q.abortion_reform_progress += 4;
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_salience += 4;
Q.progressive_credibility += 4;
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.last_policy_stage = "Negotiated concession";
Q.last_policy_authority = "Inter-party negotiation on the parliamentary timetable";
Q.last_policy_implementation = 0;
Q.news_headline = "The Left prices the common list in legislation rather than seats";
!}

The answer is a timetable, not a refusal: the two bills carried before the
campaign begins, with the votes published, and the list conversation resumed
afterwards on the basis of what actually happened. It is the only version of
the offer in which the smaller party gets paid before it gives anything up.

KO's negotiators leave without a deal and with a document they now have to
explain to their own liberal wing, which has spent fifteen years promising
these bills and has just been asked, in writing, to deliver them.

- @poland_event_queue: Send the timetable back

@ko_offer_refuse
title: Refuse and stand alone
subtitle: Independence protected at the cost of the friendliest relationship the party has.
on-arrival: {!
Q.ko_relation -= 6;
Q.spring_liberal_bridge -= 12;
Q.razem_cooperation += 6;
Q.razem_dissent -= 5;
Q.labor_dissent -= 4;
Q.barons_dissent -= 6;
Q.party_unity += 5;
Q.local_network += 3;
Q.organiser_energy += 3;
Q.left_poll_momentum += 0.10;
Q.news_headline = "The Left refuses a common list and stands on its own";
!}

The refusal is published rather than briefed, which makes it permanent. The
party will contest the election on its own name, its own threshold and its own
money, and it will be blamed loudly for every seat the right wins by a margin
smaller than the Left's vote.

It also settles an argument that had been eating the organisation from inside.
A party that has just refused to be absorbed is, for a while, unusually easy to
ask things of.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the refusal

@spring_verdict
# prose-audit: Grade A — The path closes with an authored verdict that reads the enacted reform stages, the surviving left flank and the doctrine actually chosen, then converts the record into a campaign frame rather than a score screen.
title: What the Wiosna project turned out to be
subtitle: The record before the campaign: two bills, one doctrine and whatever is left of the alliance
