        : "Neither settlement was carried. The party spent the term owning an argument it did not convert into law.");
Q.spring_verdict_flank = Q.razem_party_formed
    ? "Razem contests this election separately, and the left flank the project abandoned is on the ballot with a name."
    : (Q.razem_active && Q.razem_in_left
        ? "Razem is still inside the arrangement, which almost nobody predicted when the doctrine was adopted."
        : "There is no organised force to the party's left worth counting.");
Q.spring_verdict_doctrine = Q.spring_path_route == "market_liberal"
    ? "A fiscally conservative, socially liberal party — Ruch Postępu, attempting with a parliamentary club behind it what 2011 attempted from a television studio."
    : (Q.spring_path_route == "social_liberal"
        ? "An equality-first social-liberal party that never traded its economics for the professional vote."
        : "A party that took the leadership and never settled what it was for.");
Q.news_headline = "The Wiosna project faces its first election as itself";
!}

= August 2027 — The record, before anybody starts explaining it

The campaign begins in three weeks and the leadership has one afternoon to
decide what it is campaigning on. On the table is the only honest summary
anybody has produced.

The doctrine: **[+ spring_verdict_doctrine +]**

The laws: [+ spring_verdict_rights +]

The alliance: [+ spring_verdict_flank +]

Wiosna took a party built out of a defeated post-communist machine and a
movement that was mostly a brand, and made it into something with an argument.
Whether that argument survives its first election as the party's own property
is not decided here. What is decided here is which sentence the party says
first.

- @verdict_record
- @verdict_next

@verdict_record
title: Run on the record
subtitle: Ask to be judged on what was actually carried, and accept the judgement.
on-arrival: {!
Q.spring_path_verdict = "Ran on the record of the Wiosna project";
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.progressive_credibility += 3;
Q.left_poll_momentum += (Number(Q.spring_verdict_reforms) || 0) >= 6
    ? 0.35
    : ((Number(Q.spring_verdict_reforms) || 0) >= 3 ? 0.10 : -0.20);
Q.turnout_readiness += 3;
Q.news_headline = "The Left campaigns on the record of the Wiosna project";
!}

The leaflets carry dates and statute numbers instead of adjectives. It is the
campaign of a party that believes it did something, and it is entirely at the
mercy of whether the voters agree that what it did was the thing they needed.

- @poland_event_queue: Open the campaign

@verdict_next
title: Run on the next step
subtitle: Point past the record to what is still undone; safer where the record is thin, and it invites the obvious question.
on-arrival: {!
Q.spring_path_verdict = "Ran on the unfinished business of the Wiosna project";
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_salience += 4;
Q.public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_salience += 4;
Q.young_support += 2;
Q.urban_progressive_support += 2;
Q.left_poll_momentum += (Number(Q.spring_verdict_reforms) || 0) >= 6
    ? 0.10
    : 0.20;
Q.public_trust -= 1;
Q.turnout_readiness += 2;
Q.news_headline = "The Left campaigns on what it has not yet been allowed to finish";
!}

The campaign is built around the unfinished sentence: the bill still in
committee, the veto still on the file, the settlement that needs one more
parliament. It mobilises the people who already agree and hands every
interviewer the same question, which is what the party was doing with the term
it already had.

- @poland_event_queue: Open the campaign
